{"duration_api_ms":199122,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f29c9f14-2573-48a4-a4e0-7b02c7337c15","total_cost_usd":0.245906,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15473,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18401,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13485},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15473,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18401,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15473},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18401,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15473,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.245906,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":13485,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Every non-dominated feasible design lies on one curve: D about 3.385 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg, with only the flight-path angle varying from -1.5 to -3.568 deg. Steeper entry lowers bondline temperature (418 K to 391 K) and raises peak flux (227k to 275k W/m2) and max_g, which reaches the 12 limit at about -3.570 deg. Bluntness 1.2 and cone 70 sit at the corner of the region the aero surrogate can evaluate. Every probe beyond it (bluntness 1.205 to 1.24, or cone 69 at bluntness 1.2) failed with an extrapolation error. D is capped by the heatshield mass fraction, whose margin at D=3.385 is only 1.4e-4. The front is therefore nearly converged, and the remaining gains are small: fill gaps in gamma, push right up to the g limit, and probe a few interior points.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-e008d92646a9 (gamma -3.568) has max_g margin 0.00036, and C-2a109f1c4205 (D 3.36, gamma -3.58) has margin -0.0005. The g limit is therefore crossed near gamma -3.570.\",\"C-99ca3bd26693, C-19d0802140ac and C-e008d92646a9 give a local slope of about 1.7-1.8 g per deg. C-50a0a474d0f6 and C-960c10206981 suggest g falls with D by about 0.44 g per m.\",\"D 3.38 has mass margin 0.003097 and D 3.385 has 0.0001449, a slope of about -0.59 per m. The limit is therefore near D 3.3852.\",\"C-ea0e387c4c00, C-98457c6f78bd, C-ae614eb129f2 and C-de59f8abeee6 all failed on cd_fore extrapolation. Probes beyond bluntness 1.2 or below cone 70 at bluntness 1.2 are unsafe.\",\"C-22c8ef75dedb (D 3.2, bluntness 0.87, cone 65) has flux 322k and T 395.7 K. This is dominated by the D 3.385 family at similar gamma, so lower bluntness and smaller D cost flux.\",\"Front gaps at D 3.385 remain between the evaluated gammas -1.6/-1.8/-2.0/-2.2, -2.3/-2.6/-2.8, -2.95/-3.1/-3.25 and -3.25/-3.35/-3.42.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux falls with nose radius (bluntness x D) and with ballistic coefficient. This is prior knowledge, as I fit the exponents only roughly: flux is roughly proportional to D^-1.5 times bluntness^-0.5 to -0.7. Bondline temperature falls with steeper gamma because the soak is shorter. Peak g depends almost only on gamma, with a weak positive dependence on D. The front is therefore a one-parameter curve in gamma. It ends at the g limit on the steep side and at the -1.5 deg bound on the shallow side. Bluntness, cone and D sit at their buildable maxima. About half of this batch densifies the curve, two proposals push to the g limit and D limit, and the rest probe interior bluntness and D values to check that nothing off the curve is better.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The flux and T interpolations between evaluated gammas are reliable. The exponents for bluntness and D are from prior knowledge and are rough. The bluntness 1.0-1.15 probes could hit the surrogate convex-hull limit or have different mass-fraction behaviour. Near-limit proposals at the g and mass limits could flip to infeasible by rounding, since their margins are about 1e-5.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-a29bfeb09454\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front gap between gamma -1.6 and -1.8 at the same geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A densely covered front adds a little hypervolume.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c197169fbbea\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.8 and -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolated front point that should be non-dominated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-17412c93bd7a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.0 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239830,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6e634b66f1f6\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the large gap between gamma -2.3 and -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247850,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the widest gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-249a4f21af03\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.6 and -2.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.55,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-04c263f33850\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.8 and -2.95.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.16,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7a04ad278099\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.95 and -3.1. The earlier gamma -3.0 point used D 3.38, so this one at D 3.385 is new.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage at the exact mass-limited D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2f9f349729bd\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.1 and -3.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.18},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8d62290247ad\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.25 and -3.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.75,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-fc24e551a851\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.35 and -3.42.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.83,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-82835f5d20dc\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.42 and -3.475.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.26,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e008d92646a9\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front slightly along gamma to the g limit. The g estimate is about 11.9988, so margin is about 1e-4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5695,\"diameter_m\":3.3852},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274570,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"The largest D that just meets the mass limit, together with the steepest legal gamma, gives the lowest T on the curve. Risk is a tiny constraint flip.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e008d92646a9\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to -3.570, where g is about 11.9997. This tests how close to the g limit the front can go at D 3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274590,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.08,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Find the exact g-limited endpoint of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Probe bluntness 1.15 at cone 70, inside the surrogate hull if it is bounded by the bluntness 1.2 vertex. Flux should rise slightly. This checks whether bluntness trades off in T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":281000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether bluntness has a non-obvious benefit on T, and measures the local sensitivity to bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Probe bluntness 1.1 at cone 70 to quantify the flux sensitivity to bluntness away from the hull corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether an interior point is buildable and gauges the bluntness exponent.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Probe bluntness 1.0 at cone 70, far inside the hull, to calibrate the bluntness dependence of flux and T with low extrapolation risk.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Model calibration. It is probably dominated, but confirms the front is at the bluntness maximum.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a lower cone angle (68 deg) at bluntness 1.0 to see the cone effect on flux and mass fraction. Cone 68 at bluntness 1.0 should lie inside the hull edge running toward (0.87, 65).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":318000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the cone sensitivity in a region likely inside the aero training hull.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e008d92646a9\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D at cone 70 and bluntness 1.2 lowers g (about 0.44 per m), so gamma can be steeper. This tests whether the lower T from steeper entry offsets the higher flux. g is estimated at about 11.97.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":299000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D-dependence of T at the g limit and looks for any non-dominated point off the D-max curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e008d92646a9\",\"rationale\":\"Small D reduction (3.3) with gamma -3.58 to test a mild trade along D at the g limit, with g estimated at about 11.98.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small step in D to see whether T gains from steeper gamma can offset the higher flux.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":159865,"type":"result","duration_ms":199186,"uuid":"4124bbfa-0695-454d-b954-e49fd7a78832","ttft_stream_ms":1668,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":1668,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
